comments.body:
OK. Now with issues described in:
- https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/5214
- https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/pull/5266

I think we should revert the change and/or make it parameterized about whether to utilize. Clearly this isn't the right answer for everyone as @tonynajjar is reporting issues with acceleration constraints and @adivardi with more wobbling in the angular axis from that change.

@chanhhoang99 I followed up in #5214 for clarification on your tuning adjustments with this change. Can you follow up? 

@tonynajjar what are you plotting to get those results you posted in #5266? How would you explain this given we [apply acceleration constraints to the output optimal control](https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_mppi_controller/src/optimizer.cpp#L312-L337), regardless of the motion model? That should ensure no matter what (though quality variable) it should meed the dynamic/kinematic limitations. Is `IDX=0` somehow jumping illegitimately - I don't see any other way?

